A merge edge orders only rules whose classes both survive the merge at run
time. `merge(marginTopZero, marginAll)` drops `margin-top: 0` (the later
`margin` covers it, `Merge_key.removes`), so it orders nothing, and
`merge(marginAll, marginTopZero)` alone puts `margin: 10px` before
`margin-top: 0`. No conflict.

`base` and `wide` are in different contexts, so neither merge drops a class,
and the two merges really disagree: generate warns and keeps definition
order for that pair.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > input.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl input.ml -o output.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output.ml
